    "globalConstraints": "- The page contract, one literal for all three tasks: a page opened with no `window.__TINYAPP_SEED__` and with `window.__TINYAPP_EXAM__ === true` sets `window.__TINYAPP_STORE__` to the store it renders from, `window.__TINYAPP_DB__` to the `sqlite3.oo1.DB` handle `getDb()` resolved, and `window.__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__` to its persister only once that persister's `load()` has resolved \u2014 and creates no synchronizer and constructs no `WebSocket`. A seeded page is exactly the page it was at BASE, flag or no flag; an unseeded page without the flag is exactly the page it was at BASE \u2014 handles absent, persister and synchronizer both started. Any other global written on `window` is a finding.\n- No network: the only sockets in a persistence exam are the helper's own loopback ones \u2014 the CDP socket to the Chromium it spawned and the page's requests to the origin the helper serves on `127.0.0.1`. A request to any other origin is failed in the browser before it leaves, a `WebSocket` constructed in the page is a contract breach the exam reports, and nothing in any task reads or dials anything off the machine.\n- Every wall a persistence exam measures \u2014 `persist_ms`, `reload_ms`, the rest of `walls.json` \u2014 is reported on the record and asserted only finite and non-negative; a leg or a Check that bounds a wall is a finding (run-18, 2026-09-16).\n- A persistence exam owns its storage: one browser per exam with its own `--user-data-dir`, one loopback origin per exam with an OS-chosen port, both removed or stopped in a `finally` whatever the verdict, so two exams in one `bun test` never share a `localStorage`.\n- No schema `default` on any cell or value this plan touches, and no cell or value added: `TABLES_SCHEMA` and `VALUES_SCHEMA` are byte-for-byte what they were at BASE, so every seed and expected file on the tree \u2014 twenty snapshots at BASE \u2014 loads through `createTodosStore` to its own content.\n- The linter's four test files under `packages/tinyapp-lint/test/` keep their count and list pins loosened only to containment and tree-computed counts, never re-pinned to a new exact literal (both folds of 2026-09-15); `lint-cli.test.ts` pins the sorted list of `storeData.ts`'s callbacks, so no task exports a new function with a parameter from that module.",
